PART 5: HOW MULTIPAGE TRANSITIONS WORK UNDER V3
Per the authoritative V3_Veil_Glass_Design_Specs.md, Section 5:

The Rule
The entire application must behave as a true multipage transition app. Every view change must use the same polished motion language.

Transition Characteristics (Immutable)


Property	Value
Duration	0.6s – 0.8s
Easing	cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) or power3.out equivalents
Layering	Content moves as if it lives on the same glass surface
Scale	Very light: 0.98 → 1.0
Blur	Micro blur-to-focus: 2–3px → 0
Opacity	Smooth cross-fade between outgoing and incoming content
Coordination	Multiple elements transition together in orchestrated sequence
Where Applied
Sidebar navigation clicks — When user clicks Dashboard → Evidence: the current content dissolves out (opacity 1→0, scale 1→0.98, blur 0→2px over 0.4s), then new content dissolves in (opacity 0→1, scale 0.98→1.0, blur 2px→0 over 0.6s). The glass card, sidebar, and canvas remain stationary.

Agency View ↔ My Planner toggle — Content within the glass card cross-fades using the same 0.6-0.8s easing. No page reload, no route change — just internal state transition with the same motion language.

Internal tab/sub-view changes — Tabs within a page (e.g., Reconcile Overview → Line Items) use the same dissolve/slide. Directional hints are allowed (left→right for forward tabs, right→left for back).

Drawer open/close — Veil Drawers slide from right with 0.7s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), with strong glassmorphism backdrop.

Full route navigations — React Router route changes wrapped in a <TransitionGroup> or equivalent that applies the V3 motion characteristics. Content within the glass card transitions; the shell stays.

Content loading states — Skeleton loaders appear and cross-fade to real content using the same easing and duration.

Consistency Mandate
The same transition language must be felt on Dashboard, Evidence Center, Policy Lifecycle, Master Calendar, Taxonomy, Library, Onboarding, Admin, and every other major screen. Transitions must feel calm, elegant, and intentional — never busy or gimmicky. The motion must reinforce the single-glass illusion.

Technical Implementation Pattern
// Global transition wrapper (simplified)
const V3_TRANSITION = {
  duration: 0.7,
  ease: [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1],
  enter: { opacity: 1, scale: 1, filter: 'blur(0px)' },
  exit: { opacity: 0, scale: 0.98, filter: 'blur(2px)' },
};

// Applied to every route-level content container
<motion.div
  initial={V3_TRANSITION.exit}
  animate={V3_TRANSITION.enter}
  exit={V3_TRANSITION.exit}
  transition={{ duration: V3_TRANSITION.duration, ease: V3_TRANSITION.ease }}
>
  {/* Page content renders here */}
</motion.div>
This is not optional. It is a first-class part of the design system. Pages that don't implement it are not V3 complete.

